    <string name="control_help_title">Turn on Total control</string>
    <string name="control_help">How to turn it on</string>
    <string name="control_help_intro">Total control lets the assistant see the screen and tap, type and scroll inside other apps. For your security only you can switch it on, in Android\'s settings. It takes a minute.</string>
    <string name="control_help_on_title">Turn it on</string>
    <string name="control_help_on_1">Open Accessibility and tap “Acornix total control”. Depending on your phone it is under “Downloaded apps”, “Installed apps” or “Installed services”.</string>
    <string name="control_help_on_2">Turn on “Use Acornix total control”.</string>
    <string name="control_help_on_3">Android asks you to confirm: tap “Allow”. Done!</string>
    <string name="control_help_restricted_title">Greyed out or “Restricted setting”?</string>
    <string name="control_help_restricted_intro">Android 13 and later block this for apps installed from an APK file. You only have to unlock it once.</string>
    <string name="control_help_restricted_1">You will see Acornix greyed out, and tapping it says “App was denied access”.</string>
    <string name="control_help_restricted_2">Open Acornix\'s app info, tap ⋮ (top right) and choose “Allow restricted settings”. Confirm with your PIN or fingerprint.</string>
    <string name="control_help_restricted_3">Go back to Accessibility and turn it on as shown above.</string>
    <string name="control_help_brand_title">Xiaomi, Redmi and POCO</string>
    <string name="control_help_brand_intro">These phones close apps in the background, and that switches Total control off. Change these settings once and it will stay on.</string>
    <string name="control_help_brand_1">In “Background autostart”, search for Acornix and turn it on.</string>
    <string name="control_help_open_autostart">Open Background autostart</string>
    <string name="control_help_brand_2">In Acornix\'s app info, tap “Power”…</string>
    <string name="control_help_brand_3">…and choose “No restrictions”.</string>
    <string name="control_help_brand_4">In recent apps, long-press Acornix and tap the padlock. That way “Clear all” won\'t close it.</string>
    <string name="control_help_brand_others">On Oppo, Realme, OnePlus, Vivo, Huawei or Honor the options have similar names: look for “Autostart” or “Auto launch” and set the battery to “No restrictions” or “Unrestricted”.</string>
    <string name="control_help_stopped_title">Does it say “Total control stopped”?</string>
    <string name="control_help_stopped_text">Android still has it switched on, but the system closed Acornix. Turn it off and on again in Accessibility. If it keeps happening, check the battery and autostart settings above.</string>
